":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 86 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 12.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 7.2, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.1 to 10.1. December accounts for 14% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 7% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 5. Contract [1], for 14,807.52 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December and the high number of unique awardees do not prove improper actions. Statistical patterns can arise from market conditions or budget constraints, not wrongdoing. The data reflects trends, not violations.\nWhat can be checked: Check the December contracts for consistency with other contracts in the same period. Verify if awardee A has other contracts that might relate to the same service. Review the details of contract [1] to confirm if the amount is within standard market rates.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["GcrqouElrg7IGlsa0Wad%2Bw%3D%3D","WfXng2ucflrzAq95uGTrDQ%3D%3D","tiD1P5K%2B9ho%2FbjW6njtWLw%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}